@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title Tutorial 2 · Timing: when can the program use a synthetic Label?
hide footbox
$caller(caller, "Program\nCalls current_label")
$callee(getter, "Library\nRuns current_label")
$owner(card, "Card\nOwns its current Label")
== Case 1: program refreshes the Card first ==
caller --> getter : Call begins: lend Card until this call finishes
activate getter
getter --> caller : Call returns: lend the Card's current Label
deactivate getter
note over caller, card : Program may use this Label while Card lives and refresh has not begun.
card ->x caller : refresh_card begins: program stops using this Label
note over caller, card
  Card remains alive; access to the old Label has ended.
  After refresh finishes, the program can ask for the new Label.
end note
== Case 2: program destroys the Card without refreshing it ==
caller --> getter : Call begins: lend Card until this call finishes
activate getter
getter --> caller : Call returns: lend the Card's current Label
deactivate getter
note over caller, card : Program may use this Label while Card lives.
card ->x caller : Card is destroyed: access to this Label ends
legend bottom
  Read each case from top to bottom. Vertical gaps show order, not elapsed time.
  Person = program (caller); rectangle = library (callee); circle on base = Card (owner).
  Bar = current_label is running; dashed arrow = borrowed access.
  Cross = end of Label access. It does not mean the program is destroyed.
  Card keeps Label ownership; the program cannot pass this borrow to destroy_label.
  Non-normative: C1, C3, C5. This view covers lending; access paths are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
